{{!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     page/statement — a page that opens with a statement rather than a heading.
     Shape from NSDS templates/personal-site.html.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     The single body behind custom-about.hbs and the three page-*.hbs route
     answers. One layout, four names — the names exist because Ghost's
     template resolution and a stale routes.yaml both address templates BY
     NAME, and a name is not a reason to copy a layout. See partials/post-card.hbs
     for the same argument about cards.

     Everything is data-driven: no headline, no strapline, no image is a valid
     page and each simply does not draw.

     show_title_and_feature_image controls the WHOLE hero here, because on
     this shape the title IS the hero — an author who turns it off has written
     their own opening into the body and must not get a second one above it.
     ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}
{{#post}}
{{#if @page.show_title_and_feature_image}}
    <section class="ns-band ns-hero ns-band--dark ns-band--grid">
        <div class="ns-band__inner">
            <div class="ns-band__head">
                <h1 class="ns-band__title">{{title}}</h1>
                {{#if custom_excerpt}}<p class="ns-band__lede">{{custom_excerpt}}</p>{{/if}}
            </div>
            {{#if feature_image}}
                <img class="ns-card__media" src="{{img_url feature_image size="xl"}}"
                     srcset="{{img_url feature_image size="l"}} 1000w, {{img_url feature_image size="xl"}} 2000w"
                     sizes="(min-width: 1200px) 1200px, 100vw"
                     alt="{{#if feature_image_alt}}{{feature_image_alt}}{{/if}}">
            {{/if}}
        </div>
    </section>
{{/if}}

<section class="ns-band ns-band--tight">
    <div class="ns-band__inner">
        {{!-- gh-content AND ns-prose, both — see page.hbs for why. --}}
        <div class="gh-content ns-prose">{{content}}</div>
    </div>
</section>
{{/post}}
